The current validation is failing because of a key collision in your regex.
In your folder, every file shares the same bank and user ID (HDFC-HDFCH2H1) and only differs by the trailing sequence number (e.g., 057408, 057480, 057485). Because the previous regex only captured HDFCH2H1 as Group 1 (commonId), every new file overwrote the previous one in your groupedFiles map instead of creating separate sets for each XML and its two images.
1. Update the Regex in application.yml
Modify filename.pattern so Group 1 captures the entire unique base name (including the date and sequence number) and Group 2 still captures the 8-digit date for date validation:
filename:
  pattern: "^(MMS-(?:CREATE|CANCEL|AMEND)-[A-Z0-9]+-[A-Z0-9]+-(\\d{8})-[0-9]+)(?:-INP\\.xml|_front\\.tiff?|_detailfront\\.jpe?g)$"

How this parses your sample files:
 * MMS-CREATE-HDFC-HDFCH2H1-03092024-057408-INP.xml
 * MMS-CREATE-HDFC-HDFCH2H1-03092024-057408_front.tif
 * MMS-CREATE-HDFC-HDFCH2H1-03092024-057408_detailfront.jpg
   * Group 1 (commonId): MMS-CREATE-HDFC-HDFCH2H1-03092024-057408 — now 100% unique per transaction.
   * Group 2 (fileDateStr): 03092024 — unchanged for your 5-day date validation.
   * Suffixes: _front.tiff? matches both .tif and .tiff; _detailfront.jpe?g matches both .jpg and .jpeg.
2. Enforce Strict XML-to-Image Pairing in FileBatchingService.java
With Group 1 fixed, your groupedFiles map will now isolate each XML with its exact two matching images in a single pass. Ensure your processDirectory method checks isValidSet(folderName) before adding to completeSets so orphan XMLs or partial image sets are never batched:
// Inside FileBatchingService.processDirectory(Path subFolder)

String folderName = subFolder.getFileName().toString();
Map<String, FileSet> groupedFiles = new HashMap<>();

for (Path file : allFiles) {
    String fileName = file.getFileName().toString();

    if (outwardFileLogRepository.existsByFileNameAndErrorCodeIsNull(fileName)) {
        continue;
    }

    Matcher matcher = filePattern.matcher(fileName);
    if (!matcher.find()) {
        log.warn("Filename does not match expected pattern, skipping: {}", fileName);
        continue;
    }

    String uniqueBaseName = matcher.group(1); // e.g., MMS-CREATE-HDFC-HDFCH2H1-03092024-057408
    String fileDateStr = matcher.group(2);    // e.g., 03092024

    if (!isDateWithinAllowedRange(fileDateStr)) {
        log.warn("File date {} out of range, skipping: {}", fileDateStr, fileName);
        continue;
    }

    FileSet set = groupedFiles.computeIfAbsent(uniqueBaseName, FileSet::new);

    String lowerName = fileName.toLowerCase();
    if (lowerName.endsWith("-inp.xml")) {
        set.setXmlFile(file);
    } else if (lowerName.endsWith("_front.tif") || lowerName.endsWith("_front.tiff")) {
        set.setTifFile(file);
    } else if (lowerName.endsWith("_detailfront.jpg") || lowerName.endsWith("_detailfront.jpeg")) {
        set.setJpgFile(file);
    }
}

// Only collect pairs where the XML has both corresponding images (or XML-only for CANCEL)
List<FileSet> completeSets = groupedFiles.values().stream()
        .filter(set -> set.isValidSet(folderName))
        .toList();

No changes are needed in FileSet.isValidSet(folderName)—once uniqueBaseName includes the sequence number, every XML in CREATE and AMEND will strictly require its exact _front.tif/.tiff and _detailfront.jpg/.jpeg counterparts in the same folder to be considered valid.
